---
// REVIEW REQUIRED before app store submission.
// This policy must match the App Store privacy labels and the Google Play
// Data Safety form exactly. A mismatch is a common rejection reason.
// Children's data is involved — have this reviewed by someone qualified
// under the Australian Privacy Act, and confirm the consent arrangement
// with each school.
//
// This version has been generalized away from naming Gurmat Vidyala
// Brisbane specifically, since markAtt now supports multiple independent
// schools. The full qualified legal review is still pending — this pass
// only corrects factual accuracy (the policy no longer describes a
// single-school product) and does not constitute that review.
//
// Citizenship status is likely sensitive information under the Act, which
// requires consent rather than notice. This field is optional per school —
// confirm with each school that collects it that parents were told this
// specifically at enrolment.
//
// Retention and deletion below describe a nightly sweep and a per-student
// deletion function. Do not publish this version until both are live.
//
// Kept in the frontmatter deliberately: frontmatter is build-time only, so
// this note stays with the file without shipping in the page source.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SupportEmail from '../../components/SupportEmail.astro';
import { MARKATT, formatDate } from '../../consts';

const title = 'markAtt privacy policy';
const description =
  'What the markAtt app stores, where it is stored, and who can see it.';
const updated = MARKATT.lastUpdated;
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>markAtt privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">
      Last updated <time datetime={updated}>{formatDate(updated)}</time>
    </p>

    <h2>Who this covers</h2>
    <p>
      markAtt is used by teachers and administrators at community schools to
      mark attendance and homework. Students and parents do not use the app.
      Each school's data is kept separate: a school using markAtt can only
      see its own records, never another school's. This policy explains what
      the app stores, where it is kept, who can see it, and how long it is
      held.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app stores</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Teacher and administrator accounts.</strong> A username, a display
      name, and a role. Passwords are handled by Supabase Auth and stored
      hashed. The app never sees a plain password.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Student records.</strong> First and last name, class, a student
      number generated by the app, and — for schools that need it — whether the
      student is an Australian citizen, the name of the student's mainstream
      school, and their mainstream year level. These are entered by the school.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Parent and guardian contacts.</strong> Name, relationship to the
      student, mobile number and email address. A guardian may be linked to more
      than one student, so that families with several children are held once
      rather than repeatedly.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Attendance and homework records.</strong> One attendance mark and
      one homework mark per student per session, with the date of that session.
    </p>

    <h2>Why citizenship status is sometimes collected</h2>
    <p>
      Some schools using markAtt are required to record whether a student is an
      Australian citizen, typically for a government rebate or reporting
      requirement specific to that school. This field is optional and only used
      by schools that need it. Where it is collected, it is not used for
      anything else, it is visible only to that school's administrator, and it
      is not shared outside the school.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No advertising.</li>
      <li>No analytics and no tracking.</li>
      <li>No location data.</li>
      <li>No payments.</li>
      <li>No selling or sharing of data with third parties.</li>
      <li>No data is used to train any model.</li>
      <li>No photographs of students.</li>
      <li>No health information, and no free-text notes about students.</li>
      <li>No date of birth, home address, or medical details.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where data is stored</h2>
    <p>
      Data for all schools using markAtt is stored in Supabase, a hosted
      Postgres service, in the ap-southeast-2 region. That region is in
      Sydney, so the data stays in Australia.
    </p>

    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <p>
      Access is restricted at the database level using row-level security, not
      only in the app. A teacher can read and write records only for the classes
      they teach, and can see the guardian contacts only for students in those
      classes. A school administrator can see only their own school's records.
      No school, teacher, or administrator can see another school's records —
      this separation is enforced by the database itself, not just by the app's
      design.
    </p>
    <p>
      The developer of the app has technical access to the database, across all
      schools, in order to maintain and operate it. New schools are added to
      markAtt by the developer, not through self-service sign-up.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's information</h2>
    <p>
      Student records relate to children. Each school decides which students
      are enrolled, and each school is responsible for obtaining consent from
      parents for its own students.
    </p>
    <p>
      The app is designed to hold as little as it can. It stores what a school
      needs to mark a roll, contact a parent, and meet its own reporting
      obligations, and nothing beyond that.
    </p>
    <p>
      Consent for a school to collect and hold this information is obtained by
      that school when a student is enrolled.
    </p>
    <h2>How long it is kept</h2>
    <p>
      A student's records are kept while they are enrolled, and for two years
      after they leave. After that the record and its attendance history are
      deleted automatically. This period is applied consistently across
      schools using markAtt, to balance a school's reporting needs against
      minimizing how long personal data is held.
    </p>
    <p>
      A parent or guardian's contact details are deleted when the last student
      they are linked to is deleted.
    </p>

    <h2>Correcting or deleting a record</h2>
    <p>
      A parent or guardian can ask their child's school to correct or delete
      their child's record at any time, and can ask what is held about their
      child. Requests can go to the school directly, or to <SupportEmail />.
    </p>
    <p>
      When a student's record is deleted, their attendance and homework marks,
      their class history, and their link to any guardian are deleted with it. A
      guardian's contact details are deleted if no other student is linked to
      them.
    </p>

    <h2>If something goes wrong</h2>
    <p>
      If data held in markAtt is exposed or accessed by someone who should not
      have seen it, the affected school will be told, and affected families
      will be told where the risk of harm makes that appropriate. Where the law
      requires it, the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner will
      be notified.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions and requests</h2>
    <p>
      Email <SupportEmail /> with any question about this policy. This is the
      same address as the <a href="/markatt/support/">markAtt support page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted here with a new
      last-updated date. Where a change affects what is collected or how long it
      is kept, affected schools will be told directly.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>